# Same SPA rule as netlify.toml, but inside the published folder.
#
# netlify.toml lives at the repo root and only applies to a git-connected
# build. A drag-and-drop deploy uploads dist/ alone, so it never sees it --
# and every route except / would 404. Vite copies public/ into dist/, so this
# travels with the build either way.
#
# Real files are served before this is consulted, so assets are unaffected.
/*  /index.html  200
